speechtext:
No, Mr. Speaker, I have not seen the correspondence, but I am not too concerned about that. I understand from the press that the premier of Quebec has indicated to the city of Montreal that they have his authority to enter into a slum clearance arrangement under the statute. I expected that my hon. friend might ask such a question this morning, and I brought a copy of the statute along with me. It states in section 23 that the federal government is empowered to enter into slum clearance arrangements with any municipality, subject to section 23 (3) (a), which states:
No grant shall be paid to a municipality under this section unless (a) the government of the province in which the area is situated has approved the acquisition and clearance thereof by the municipality;
I understand that the premier of Quebec has said that he will approve but I have seen nothing in writing. However, I am not too concerned about that. I understand it will be forthcoming.

Membership is by no means a condition of employment.
50433-413}
Supply-Transport
